    "id": "pavilion-square-kl-review",
    "slug": "pavilion-square-kl-review",
    "title": "Pavilion Square KL Review: Price, Layouts, Pros & Cons",
    "metaDescription": "Pavilion Square review: 67-storey residences with a dedicated link bridge to Pavilion KL, from RM 1.7 million. Layouts, facilities, fees, pros and cons.",
    "summary": "Pavilion Square is a 67-storey tower of 960 residences on Jalan Raja Chulan, with its own link bridge into Pavilion Kuala Lumpur. This review covers price, the eight layouts, the rooftop pool and sky sports zone, the leasehold question, and who it suits.",
    "content": "# Quick verdict: who should buy Pavilion Square?\n\n**My view.** What you buy at Pavilion Square is the Pavilion name and the bridge. The tower stands behind the Royale Chulan hotel, between KL City Centre, TRX and KL Tower, and a private air-conditioned link bridge takes you into Pavilion KL in a few minutes; the Bukit Bintang MRT is about six minutes on foot. Pavilion Group has completed every project it has launched, which matters to me when a building is this large. Two things stood out when I filmed the show units: every home is delivered fully fitted, with marble floors, branded appliances and furniture, and the larger layouts have a balcony, which many Kuala Lumpur city-centre projects do not offer. North-facing units look towards the Twin Towers and south-facing units over Bukit Bintang. The trade-offs are leasehold tenure and 960 units in one tower; if freehold is a must, compare it with CloutHaus or Orion.\n\n- **Suits:** buyers who want direct mall access and the Pavilion brand; owners who want a wide choice from studio to 3 bedrooms.\n- **Think twice if:** freehold is a must, or you prefer a low-density building.\n\n# Video walkthrough\n\n{{youtube:Ip9wDev_pF4}}\n\n# Pavilion Square at a glance\n\n| Item | Detail |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Developer | Armani Hartajaya Sdn Bhd (Pavilion Group) |\n| Address | Lot 297, Jalan Raja Chulan, 50200 Kuala Lumpur |\n| Tenure | Leasehold |\n| Land size | 2.023 acres |\n| Residential tower | 67 storeys, 960 residences |\n| Units per floor / lifts | 20 units, 12 lifts |\n| Other components | 25-storey tower with 106 corporate suites, retail lots |\n| Built-up | 504 to 1,272 sq ft |\n| Layouts | Studio to 3 bedrooms |\n| Price | From RM 1.7 million |\n| Maintenance fee | RM 0.90 psf |\n| Target completion | 2029 (58 months) |\n\n# Where is Pavilion Square, and what is nearby?\n\nOn Jalan Raja Chulan in the Golden Triangle. The link bridge goes to Pavilion Kuala Lumpur; The Starhill, Fahrenheit88 and Lot 10 follow from there. Bukit Bintang MRT, Conlay MRT and the Raja Chulan and Bukit Bintang monorail stations serve the area, and the covered Bukit Bintang to KL City Centre walkway leads to Suria Mall. Prince Court Medical Centre and Tung Shin Hospital are the nearest hospitals.\n\n# How does Pavilion Square compare with its neighbours?\n\n| Project | Tenure | From | Built-up | Units | Monthly fee |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Pavilion Square** | Leasehold | RM 1.7 million | 504 to 1,272 sq ft | 960 | RM 0.90 psf |\n| [CloutHaus](/projects/clouthaus) | Freehold | RM 1.5 million | 549 to 1,216 sq ft | 615 | RM 0.80 psf |\n| [Orion Residence](/projects/orion-residence) | Freehold | RM 1.58 million | 491 to 1,329 sq ft | 298 | RM 1.32 psf |\n| [Core Residence @ TRX](/projects/core-residence-trx) | Freehold | RM 1.5 million | 622 to 1,572 sq ft | 700 | ask |\n\n# Which Pavilion Square layout is best?\n\n| Type | Size | Configuration |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| A | 504 sq ft | Studio, 1 bathroom |\n| B1 / B2 | 770 to 772 sq ft | 1 + 1 bedrooms |\n| C1 | 966 sq ft | 2 bedrooms, 2 bathrooms |\n| C2 | 978 sq ft | 2 + 1 bedrooms |\n| C3 | 1,100 sq ft | 2 + 1 bedrooms |\n| C4 | 1,272 sq ft | 2 + 1 bedrooms |\n| D | 1,255 sq ft | 3 bedrooms, 3 bathrooms |\n\n**What I would pick.** The 1,272 sq ft two-plus-one (Type C4) is the unit I filmed and the one I would choose for a family: a dining area that seats eight to ten, a study large enough to become a third bedroom, a walk-in wardrobe and a bathtub in the master suite. For one person or a couple, the 1 + 1 (Type B) is the sensible middle, with the extra room as a study; Type D is the only true three-bedroom. The 504 sq ft studio comes with a fitted kitchen and a concealed fridge and works as a city base.\n\n# Facilities\n\nLevel 12 has the club lounge, reading room, KTV, business centre, kids' room, BBQ plaza and courtyard garden. Level 63A is a 15,000 sq ft sky wellness zone with gym, outdoor gym, steam and sauna, which the developer describes as the highest and largest sky sports zone in KL city centre. Level 67 holds the 118-metre rooftop infinity pool, described as the highest and longest in the city centre, plus kids', wading and jacuzzi pools. Level 66 is a sky garden.\n\n# Pros and cons\n\n| Pros | Cons |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Dedicated link bridge to Pavilion KL | Leasehold |\n| Pavilion Group brand and track record in the area | 960 units and 20 units per floor: a busy building |\n| 118-metre rooftop pool and 15,000 sq ft sky wellness zone | RM 0.90 psf monthly fee |\n| Full range from studio to 3 bedrooms | Completion in 2029 |\n\n# How to view Pavilion Square\n\nWhatsApp Shyan Yee (REN 46305, IQI Realty) at +60 10-827 8932 for the price list, floor plans and a viewing. Full specifications are on the [Pavilion Square project page](/projects/pavilion-square-residences).\n\nFor the full unit-type table, facilities list and nearby distances, see the [Pavilion Square data page on PropertyPortal](https://www.propertyportal.my/project/pavilion-square-residences).",
